\title{bootstrict: Strict Bootstrap 5.3 Widgets for Shiny}
\description{
\code{bootstrict} re-implements the Bootstrap 5.3 layout, content, forms and
component library as Shiny UI functions. Each widget mirrors the Bootstrap
5.3 HTML structure one-to-one, theming is delegated to \code{bslib} (which ships
the Bootstrap 5.3 runtime, so a designer's SASS variable sheet drops
straight in) and interactive components report their state to the server,
with server-side \verb{update_*()} controls.
}
\section{Conventions}{

\itemize{
\item Every constructor is \code{snake_case} and prefixed \code{bs_} (e.g. \code{\link[=bs_card]{bs_card()}}).
\item \code{...} follows the Shiny/htmltools convention: named arguments become HTML
attributes, unnamed arguments become children. Extra \code{class} values passed
through \code{...} are merged with the component's own classes. Bootstrap's
utility classes are therefore written as themselves rather than wrapped in
arguments, so a mockup's \code{class} list transfers verbatim.
\item Interactive constructors take a leading \code{id} so their value is available as
\code{input$id}. Where a component is useful without one -- an alert, a nav, a
dropdown -- the \code{id} is optional and the widget stays static markup until
it is given one.
\item Server helpers take the \code{id} first and the \code{session} last and optional,
and namespace the id themselves inside a Shiny module. The UI triggers
(\code{\link[=bs_modal_trigger]{bs_modal_trigger()}} and friends) point at a target element, so those
need \code{ns()} applied by the caller.
}
}

\section{Known deviations}{

If it is not in the Bootstrap documentation it is not in \code{bootstrict}, even
where that loses a Shiny feature. One thing falls short, inherited from the
Shiny inputs the package delegates to: every delegated input keeps Shiny's
\code{div.form-group.shiny-input-container} wrapper, which is why validation
feedback needs \code{\link[=bs_feedback]{bs_feedback()}} rather than a bare \code{\link[=bs_invalid_feedback]{bs_invalid_feedback()}}
placed after the control. No third-party widget library is shipped.
}

